{"name":"Blue Chamber","hex":"#5671a7","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue chamber","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A forbidden room."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue_chamber"}],"entries":[{"title":"National Assembly of Quebec","blocks":[{"text":"The National Assembly of Quebec is the legislative body of the province of Quebec in Canada. Legislators are called MNAs. The lieutenant governor of Quebec and the National Assembly compose the Parliament of Quebec, which operates in a fashion similar to those of other Westminster-style parliamentary systems. The assembly has 127 members elected via first past the post from single-member districts."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Assembl%C3%A9e_nationale_du_Qu%C3%A9bec_1.svg/330px-Assembl%C3%A9e_nationale_du_Qu%C3%A9bec_1.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Assembly_of_Quebec"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/National_A